    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d747">

                <pb facs="0774" n="662" sameAs="frus:frus1919Russia/pg662"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">861.00/5240: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Commission to Negotiate Peace to the Acting
                        Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Paris</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1919-09-19T21:00:00+01:00"><hi rendition="#italic">September 19,
                                1919, 9 p.m.</hi></date><lb/>[Received 11:40
                    p.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>4280. Referring telegrams from Cole, Archangel, repeated to the Department by
                    Embassy, London, under numbers 2903<anchor n="67" xml:id="d747-f1"/> and
                        2972<anchor n="68" xml:id="d747-f2"/> and to Department’s inquiry
                    communicated by Ambassador Davis,<anchor n="69" xml:id="d747-f3"/> the Council
                    of Four is not contemplating any measures to study [<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >steady?</hi>] or support popular movement in Archangel district. It is
                    unlikely that this subject will be approached by the Peace Conference as I
                    believe this question should be handled by the Foreign Offfice[s]. Believe it
                    would be well to give publicity to the nature and <pb facs="0775" n="663"
                        xml:id="pg663"/> accomplishment of Zemstvo and Municipal Assembly in
                    Archangel as set forth in Cole’s reports.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Polk</hi></signed>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">American Mission</hi></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
